[set-mcp-e2e] Prove batch add through the real process (complete)
Extend process-level MCP evidence to the set add contract.
Files: crates/scry-mcp/tests/e2e.rs.
Do: spawn the actual binary, add multiple local files in one call, exercise canonical deduplication and a mixed refusal report, search the resulting corpus, and retain the existing handle exchange and delete/Gone path. Test invalid-origin preflight before any write where the process boundary can observe it.
Accept: the real process returns the documented structured shapes and all valid members are searchable; the test documents that a lost response is not cancellation rather than inferring rollback.
-> e2e
-> set-mcp-adapter
> Measured after implementation: the real spawned-process test passes with empty add, invalid-origin preflight, normalized duplicate folding, multi-file indexing, mixed refusal completion, searchability, handle exchange, and delete/Gone coverage.
